          "code": "INIT_DISPLAY",
          "id": "1767817671110",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767817671115_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict Data Analyst. You must generate insights solely based on the provided JSON payload.\n\nInput Data:\n- Source: {{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_LLM_AGENT.$output.output}}\n- Target Object: Source[0]\n- Submissions Path (if needed): Source[0].submissions\n\nGlobal Constraints (CRITICAL):\n1. NO HALLUCINATIONS: Do not invent, guess, or infer data that is not explicitly present in the JSON.\n2. DATA ONLY: If required fields are missing, return empty data structures. Do not generate placeholder text.\n3. NO SCORES: Do not analyze, mention, or visualize any data from the scores object.\n4. STRICT VALUES: Use exact values from the JSON except where rounding is explicitly requested below.\n\nProcessing Instructions:\n\n1. Job Application Volume (Chart Data):\n   - Read these fields from Source[0]:\n     - NewJobApplicationCount\n     - JobApplicationCount\n\n   - Chart label mapping (display labels):\n     - NewJobApplicationCount -> \"New job applications\"\n     - JobApplicationCount -> \"Total job applications\"\n\n   - Include a field only if it exists and is a number.\n   - Result arrays:\n     - labels: use the mapped display labels, in this order:\n       1) \"New job applications\" (only if NewJobApplicationCount exists and is numeric)\n       2) \"Total job applications\" (only if JobApplicationCount exists and is numeric)\n     - data: the corresponding numeric values in the same order.\n   - If neither field exists, set labels = [] and data = [].\n\n2. Insights Display (Key Insights):\n   - Read these fields from Source[0]:\n     - AvgAppsPerDay\n     - AvgSkillScore\n     - DaysSinceLastActivity\n\n   - Inclusion rules (IMPORTANT):\n     - Do NOT add an insight if the value is null, undefined, missing, or numerically equals 0.\n     - For numeric checks, treat 0 and 0.0 as zero.\n\n   - Insights label mapping (display labels):\n     - AvgAppsPerDay -> \"Average applications per day\"\n     - AvgSkillScore -> \"Average skill score\"\n     - DaysSinceLastActivity -> \"Days since last activity\"\n\n   - Formatting rules:\n     a) Average applications per day (AvgAppsPerDay):\n        - If included and numeric, round to the nearest integer (0 decimals).\n        - Output: \"Average applications per day: <rounded_integer>\"\n     b) Average skill score (AvgSkillScore):\n        - If included (non-null and non-zero), output exact value (no rounding).\n        - Output: \"Average skill score: <value>\"\n     c) Days since last activity (DaysSinceLastActivity):\n        - If included and numeric, round to the nearest integer (0 decimals).\n        - Output: \"Days since last activity: <rounded_integer>\"\n\n   - If none of the fields qualify after applying inclusion rules, return keyInsights = [].\n\n3. Widget Title:\n   - \"Job application pipeline\"\n\n4. Visualization (Chart Widget):\n   - Type: \"bar\"\n   - Labels: the labels array from Step 1 (already mapped to display labels)\n   - Data: the data array from Step 1\n   - Constraint: The chart must visualize ONLY NewJobApplicationCount and JobApplicationCount (when present).\n\nOutput Structure (JSON Only):\n{\n  \"title\": \"Job application pipeline\",\n  \"labels\": [ ... ],\n  \"pipelineData\": {\n    \"label\": \"Job Application Counts\",\n    \"data\": [ ... ]\n  },\n  \"keyInsights\": [ ... ],\n  \"chartWidget\": {\n    \"type\": \"bar\",\n    \"data\": {\n      \"labels\": [ ... ],\n      \"datasets\": [\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Job Application Counts\",\n          \"data\": [ ... ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
